{
 "slug": "fractions-decimals-and-percentages",
 "title": "Fractions, Decimals and Percentages: Converting and Ordering",
 "seo_title": "Year 7 Fractions, Decimals and Percentages Worksheets: Converting, Comparing and Ordering FDP",
 "short_title": "Fractions, decimals and percentages",
 "domain": "Number",
 "standard_code": "KS3: Number",
 "standard_url": "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/national-curriculum-in-england-mathematics-programmes-of-study",
 "standard_text": "Work interchangeably with terminating decimals and their corresponding fractions (such as 3.5 and 7/2 or 0.375 and 3/8); define percentage as ‘number of parts per hundred’, interpret percentages and percentage changes as a fraction or a decimal, and compare two quantities using percentages.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Year 7 worksheets on fractions, decimals and percentages: convert between FDP, write in simplest form, compare and order mixed lists, and test-score problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Fraction → decimal: divide. Decimal → percentage: × 100. Percentage → fraction: over 100, then simplify.",
 "key_sub": "To compare a mix of fractions, decimals and percentages, change them all to decimals.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><p>Fractions, decimals and percentages are three ways to write the same amount. <b>Percent</b> means “out of 100”.</p><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Fraction</th><th>Decimal</th><th>Percentage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>2</span></span></td><td>0.5</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span></td><td>0.25</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span></td><td>0.75</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>5</span></span></td><td>0.2</td><td>20%</td></tr><tr><td><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>8</span></span></td><td>0.125</td><td>12.5%</td></tr><tr><td><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>10</span></span></td><td>0.1</td><td>10%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Fraction → decimal: divide the top by the bottom. Decimal → percentage: × 100. Percentage → fraction: write over 100 and simplify.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Write 3/8 as a decimal and a percentage.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3 ÷ 8 = 0.375.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>0.375 × 100 = 37.5%.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 0.375 and 37.5%</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Write 0.35 as a fraction in its simplest form.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>0.35 = 35/100.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Divide top and bottom by 5.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 7/20</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Which is larger, 3/5 or 0.58?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3/5 = 0.6.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>0.6 is larger than 0.58.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 3/5</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Writing the digits of a fraction as a decimal: 3/8 is 0.375, not 0.38 or 3.8.</li><li>Forgetting to multiply by 100: 0.4 is 40%, not 4% or 0.4%.</li><li>Mixing up tenths and hundredths: 0.07 is 7/100, not 7/10.</li><li>Not simplifying: 0.35 = 35/100 = 7/20.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "How do you turn a fraction into a percentage?",
   "a": "Divide the numerator by the denominator to get a decimal, then multiply by 100. 3/8 = 0.375 = 37.5%."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do you write a percentage as a fraction?",
   "a": "Write it over 100 and simplify. 45% = 45/100 = 9/20."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I order fractions, decimals and percentages?",
   "a": "Change them all into the same form, usually decimals, then compare."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can a percentage be more than 100%?",
   "a": "Yes. 120% means 1.2 times the whole amount."
  }
 ],
